## What B was

```
-    await this.settleSubmitted(() => {
+    const settled = await this.settleSubmitted(() => {
       const response = responses[index];
       if (!response) throw new TransactionError(…);
-      answered(response);
+      return response;
     });
+    answered(settled);
```

The SAME answer, stated by the same caller, one statement later — outside the
region in which the hold is released. Exactly the two combined-failure cells go
red again; every other cell of the file stays green, including the four D-65
cardinality answers (which have no listener) and the successful-answer +
failed-listener control. So what closes the defect is the POSITION inside
`settleSubmitted`, not the fact that `capturedMutation` now takes the answer.

